---
kind: scene
id: east.lanternNight
title: Lantern night
on: enterPlace
target: place.ashTowerHall
also: true
once: day
when: "clock.weekday == 4 && @isNight"
---

// Friday nights (clock.weekday == 4) Ashgrove carries its lanterns up to the
// tower. An `also` beat: it plays after the hall's own beat, or alone. What
// the town can do depends on the siege.

## The procession

::bg{location="ash-tower-hall" time="night"}
::music{action="change" mood="calm" volume="down"}
@narrator: It is Friday night, and Ashgrove comes up the hill with its lanterns: paper moons on sticks, one for every monster the town has lost.
<match on="run.lair.towerSiege">
  <when is="cleared">
    @narrator: This week they climb all the way to the top. The bells ring once for each lantern, and nobody touches the ropes.
    ::auto{character="elderRook" anchor="center" action="enter"}
    @elderRook{emotion="happy"}: There you are. Carry one up for me, would you? My knees have not forgiven those grunts.
  </when>
  <otherwise>
    @narrator: This week they stop in the hall. Nobody will go past the third step, and nobody says why.
    ::auto{character="ashgroveLanternMaker" anchor="center" action="enter"}
    @ashgroveLanternMaker: Elder Rook always carries the first lantern. We're carrying his, too, until he comes down.
  </otherwise>
</match>
@narrator: You are handed a lantern. It is warm, and very light, and it does not go out.
